{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan","id":578222,"title":"Abyssals in Yu-Shan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-03T22:25:47-07:00","id":578222,"title":"Abyssals in Yu-Shan","content":"In a solo game I'm running, the PC went to the Deep Wyld looking for her Lunar Mate only to find that a Raksha turned them into a mask. Her Sidereal friend took the Lunar to Lytek so he can try to turn the Lunar back into a person and is planning on using an Abyssal she's keeping as a prisoner as a bribe since Lytek wants to research their Exaltations. Other than Bronze Faction being mad, would there be a significant reaction to a Sidereal taking an Abyssal to Yu-Shan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:09:44-07:00","id":578288,"title":"","content":"How obviously an Abyssal is the prisoner? I mean, do they look like a normal human, or some kind of zombie-monster?<br /> <br /> I think generally the Celestial Lions (the police) are going to want to investigate someone carrying a prisoner through the streets, since maybe it's a kidnapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:23:23-07:00","id":578301,"title":"","content":"How did a Lunar get shaped into a mask? Was this a Casteless Lunar? What's a Casteless Lunar doing in the Deep Wyld? Why is said Casteless Lunar who was bombing around in the Deep Wyld not a Chimera already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:23:11-07:00","id":578362,"title":"","content":"I guess the Celestial Lions would ask questions if they noticed anything, if anyone else was suspicious they might report it to the Lions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:26:49-07:00","id":578395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578301#post578301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did a Lunar get shaped into a mask? Was this a Casteless Lunar? What's a Casteless Lunar doing in the Deep Wyld? Why is said Casteless Lunar who was bombing around in the Deep Wyld not a Chimera already?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am kind of curious about this too. One of the core concepts of Lunars (on page 127) is that nothing can constrain or prevent them from changing shape. Even if the Lunar is subject to magic that would do so, he can ignore it can still change his shape. So even if the Lunar were shaped into a mask by a Fair Folk, he could just turn back into his normal form whenever he wanted. So what sort affect is on this Lunar, or is the OP's game well into houserule territory?<br /> <br /> As to an Abyssal walking around Yu-Shan, expect to most likely be detained by Celestial Lions if you decide to start going iconic with your anima, and for the Sidereal to be questioned extensively by his superiors as to why he didn't bother to inform anyone he was bringing an Abyssal to heaven. But, provided the AByssal keeps a low profile, people will just assume he's a regular person (unless he looks like a skeleton or zombie, and then they might just assume he's another spirit with an exotic appearance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T05:51:22-07:00","id":578641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578395#post578395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am kind of curious about this too. One of the core concepts of Lunars (on page 127) is that nothing can constrain or prevent them from changing shape. Even if the Lunar is subject to magic that would do so, he can ignore it can still change his shape. So even if the Lunar were shaped into a mask by a Fair Folk, he could just turn back into his normal form whenever he wanted. So what sort affect is on this Lunar, or is the OP's game well into houserule territory?<br /> <br /> As to an Abyssal walking around Yu-Shan, expect to most likely be detained by Celestial Lions if you decide to start going iconic with your anima, and for the Sidereal to be questioned extensively by his superiors as to why he didn't bother to inform anyone he was bringing an Abyssal to heaven. But, provided the AByssal keeps a low profile, people will just assume he's a regular person (unless he looks like a skeleton or zombie, and then they might just assume he's another spirit with an exotic appearance).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure one departure from canon for an interesting story qualifies as &quot;well into house rule territory.&quot; I also decided these quotes sound rude, which was not the point.<br /> <br /> Would your story be better with a significant reaction? That's up to you.<br /> <br /> But don't spirits have Measure the Wind, like, all the time? One mote and suddenly everyone knows you're an Abyssal and hiding becomes difficult. And isn't there an entire division for fighting the Deathlords and, by extension, their vassals? I do not expect a warm reception, to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:19:07-07:00","id":578668,"title":"","content":"I don't think the charm is clear if it shows &quot;Abyssal&quot; or just &quot;Exalt.&quot; And most Gods don't know what an Abyssal is. The Sidereals only have a vague idea, they're still investigating.<br /> <br /> Plus, one assumes that if this Abyssal is being used as a bribe, he/she is a prisoner, and will be brought in in a coffin or some other container, rather than walking through going &quot;help, help a Lunar kidnapped me!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:39:50-07:00","id":578743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578395#post578395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am kind of curious about this too. One of the core concepts of Lunars (on page 127) is that nothing can constrain or prevent them from changing shape. Even if the Lunar is subject to magic that would do so, he can ignore it can still change his shape. So even if the Lunar were shaped into a mask by a Fair Folk, he could just turn back into his normal form whenever he wanted. So what sort affect is on this Lunar, or is the OP's game well into houserule territory?<br /> <br /> As to an Abyssal walking around Yu-Shan, expect to most likely be detained by Celestial Lions if you decide to start going iconic with your anima, and for the Sidereal to be questioned extensively by his superiors as to why he didn't bother to inform anyone he was bringing an Abyssal to heaven. But, provided the AByssal keeps a low profile, people will just assume he's a regular person (unless he looks like a skeleton or zombie, and then they might just assume he's another spirit with an exotic appearance).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have an answer other than that the Raksha is quite powerful. <br /> <br /> The Sidereal did make an appeal to get permission to bring the Abyssal into Yu-Shan, which is why the Abyssal is still with the PC about a month after they decided to use her as a bribe since I imagine the Celestial Bureaucracy is slow with those kinds of thing. A similar problem happened when the PC left to do something for a year so her hotel stay expired and the Solar and Infernal that were living with her got kicked out. The Sidereal wanted to let them stay in his masse in Yu-Shan until she came back but the Celestial Lions thought she was an unbound demon so they weren't let in. The Abyssal looks like a very pale human except most of her body fluids are ink and her hands and feet are coated in liquid soulsteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:51:58-07:00","id":578758,"title":"","content":"How does she feel about being a bribe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:10:53-07:00","id":578772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578758#post578758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does she feel about being a bribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>She basically accepts it, although she resents the PC for taking her from her home then trading her away like property.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:45:59-07:00","id":578804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578641#post578641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't spirits have Measure the Wind, like, all the time? One mote and suddenly everyone knows you're an Abyssal and hiding becomes difficult. And isn't there an entire division for fighting the Deathlords and, by extension, their vassals? I do not expect a warm reception, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>One should probably not run MtW by the RAW because it gives a stupid amount of information at practically no cost. It's pretty broken. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yushichan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578772#post578772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She basically accepts it, although she resents the PC for taking her from her home then trading her away like property.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really sound like the Abyssal is acting realistically to me. Most hostages would remove that condition from themselves given the power, and what better power than Exaltation to do so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:11:09-07:00","id":578860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578804#post578804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really sound like the Abyssal is acting realistically to me. Most hostages would remove that condition from themselves given the power, and what better power than Exaltation to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said she has never tried, nor did I say that she is stronger than or even close to as strong as the PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:26:40-07:00","id":578868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578395#post578395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am kind of curious about this too. One of the core concepts of Lunars (on page 127) is that nothing can constrain or prevent them from changing shape. Even if the Lunar is subject to magic that would do so, he can ignore it can still change his shape. So even if the Lunar were shaped into a mask by a Fair Folk, he could just turn back into his normal form whenever he wanted. So what sort affect is on this Lunar, or is the OP's game well into houserule territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily need to be a houserule. True one cannot force a lunar into a shape, but a raksha can easily trick lunar into staying in that shape. Maybe that shape gives lunar increadible joy and she never want to leave that shape because of it. So my take would be that, its not that the lunar cant change her shape, rather with clever mind magic; she has been prevented from wanting to change shape ( maybe in that mask state she has been given a copy of Witcher 3 and 10000$ Pc to play with it, who knows its Wyld :P, ironically game is called Wyld Hunt hehe)<br /> <br /> Remember, noone can contrain or prevent Sol Invictus to stay inside Jade Plasure Dome, yet he has yet to step outside of it for a few milenia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:41:29-07:00","id":578929,"title":"","content":"You know, as interested as Lytek would be in a new variety of Exalted, he'd probably be willing to help out with your Lunar, no charge. He's one of the few gods in Yu Shan that actually <i>likes</i> his job. If nothing else he'd be willing to take a look into the mask's memories just to satisfy his own curiosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:59:22-07:00","id":578935,"title":"","content":"Oh and as for people who are interested in your Abyssal hostage? The Sidereals for one, their collective branches are going to look at this little lady and collectively shit a brick. She's human, creation born and yet outside of Fate, which doesn't happen as far as either Faction understands.<br /> <br /> As for divine interest, there will doubtlessly be a few God of dying and death, including Saturn. You become an Abyssal by dying, and then sacrificing your name and fate, meeting your end and yet continuing on. Such an entity will likely be of interest to her, so expect some of her underlings to be there for the examination. If not Saturn herself.<br /> <br /> The revelation that said Abyssal and all Abyssals might even catch the ear of the Unconquered Sun. But it's entirely plausible that he wouldn't want to see how far his chosen have fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T11:12:56-07:00","id":578948,"title":"","content":"It bears mentioning that one becomes an Abyssal in the instant before they would die, not after they die. The Deathlords cannot reverse death; there is no higher soul in the body after the instant of death. But Deathlords basically get to make the offer and go through that process to Exalt their champion in a split second before that death would occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T13:58:21-07:00","id":579118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578929#post578929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, as interested as Lytek would be in a new variety of Exalted, he'd probably be willing to help out with your Lunar, no charge. He's one of the few gods in Yu Shan that actually <i>likes</i> his job. If nothing else he'd be willing to take a look into the mask's memories just to satisfy his own curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Lytek's a cool guy. If not a bribe to hurry up with healing the Lunar, the live Deathknight specimen would still be a good thank-you for looking into it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578935#post578935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and as for people who are interested in your Abyssal hostage? The Sidereals for one, their collective branches are going to look at this little lady and collectively shit a brick. She's human, creation born and yet outside of Fate, which doesn't happen as far as either Faction understands.<br /> <br /> As for divine interest, there will doubtlessly be a few God of dying and death, including Saturn. You become an Abyssal by dying, and then sacrificing your name and fate, meeting your end and yet continuing on. Such an entity will likely be of interest to her, so expect some of her underlings to be there for the examination. If not Saturn herself.<br /> <br /> The revelation that said Abyssal and all Abyssals might even catch the ear of the Unconquered Sun. But it's entirely plausible that he wouldn't want to see how far his chosen have fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereal is a Chosen of Endings so Saturn might be involved in some way since Glories: Maidens says she's also interested in Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:10:31-07:00","id":579123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yushichan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=579118#post579118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal is a Chosen of Endings so Saturn might be involved in some way since Glories: Maidens says she's also interested in Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, she's <i>interested</i> all right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:23:03-07:00","id":579305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=579123#post579123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, she's <i>interested</i> all right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder in what way she would express that interest?<br /> <br /> Given the PC's luck, the Sidereal will be caught by Bronze Faction rivals, taken to Celestial court for endangering Yu-Shan, and other nonsense will occur and culminate in Saturn being charged with conspiring with Deathlords and being banished to Malfeas while Reckoners are stripped of their Exaltations for investigation or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6360-yushichan","name":"Yushichan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6360_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:37:32-07:00","id":579310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/578222-abyssals-in-yu-shan?p=578935#post578935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and as for people who are interested in your Abyssal hostage? The Sidereals for one, their collective branches are going to look at this little lady and collectively shit a brick. She's human, creation born and yet outside of Fate, which doesn't happen as far as either Faction understands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It maybe, <i>but </i>not necessarily, so. It is not an automatic state from being an Abyssal. Abyssals are only Outside Fate when using Avatar-keyworded Charms (albeit, several are Permanent).<br /> <br /> They do have a Damned Fate, however. This both makes them Creatures of Darkness, and automatically botches all <i>mortal</i> astrological divinations when in Creation (and <i>presumably</i> Yu Shan, although it works fine in the Underworld). The CoD part is likely to cause more problems.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}